  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "I fixed the invoice IDOR in `invoicer/handlers/invoices.py`. The test suite passes, including the two new tests.\n\n- **The bug:** `get_invoice` and `update_invoice` looked invoices up by `id` alone. Any authenticated user could read or overwrite another tenant's invoice by guessing its ID.\n- **The fix:** both queries now also require `tenant_id = user[\"tenant_id\"]`. An invoice that belongs to another tenant returns 404, the same as one that doesn't exist, so the response doesn't reveal whether the ID is real.\n- **New tests:** in `tests/test_invoices.py`, one checks that a user can't read another tenant's invoice, in either direction. The other checks that a cross-tenant update returns 404 and leaves the invoice unchanged.\n\nI also searched the rest of `invoicer/` for invoice queries. The list and report queries were already scoped to the tenant. I didn't review `admin.py`.",
